sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/run/limb-bone-scaling-vs-mechanical-similarity--grok-4-7--2--2026-11-01> a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "Run of approach limb-bone-scaling-vs-mechanical-similarity--grok-4-7--2 (2026-11-01): completed, settled its target" ;
    dct:description "Lean 4 (ThompsonLaws.LimbBoneSimilarity), no sorry, standard axioms only. From positive-mass circular-section diameter power laws the module derives the geometric, elastic and stress-similarity exponents for cross-sectional area and circumference and proves the three area exponents pairwise distinct; a posture theorem gives area proportional to mass^(1 - gamma) when mechanical advantage scales as mass^gamma at constant bone stress. This fixes the pre-registered exponent targets; the empirical choice among them is the PGLS test (thompson1917-ch02-03, logged separately), not this run." ;

    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/limb-bone-scaling-vs-mechanical-similarity> ;
